---
import StoreLayout from '../layouts/StoreLayout.astro';
import '../styles/store.css';
import Hero from '../assets/blog-placeholder-about.jpg';
---
<StoreLayout title="About Me" description="I am the UI/UX designer and lead developer behind Agentic Fashion">
	<div class="about-page">
		<section class="page-head">
			<h1>About Me</h1>
			<p class="page-head__subtitle">
				I'm the UI/UX designer and lead developer behind Agentic Fashion — the part of
				this store where the clothes meet the way you actually feel about them. I care
				about how shopping should feel, so everything here is built to feel like a calm,
				intentional wardrobe rather than a boring product list.
			</p>
		</section>

		<section class="about-hero">
			<div class="about-hero__media">
				<img src={Hero.src} alt="A stylized Agentic Fashion garment on an intentional wardrobe-inspired gradient" width="100%" height="auto" loading="eager" />
			</div>
			<div class="about-hero__caption">
				<span class="about-hero__eyebrow">The Agentic Fashion team</span>
				<p>Design, AI guidance, and the quiet details that make a wardrobe feel like it was made for you.</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section>
			<div class="section-heading">Who I work with</div>
			<ul class="about-list">
				<li>
					<h3>UI/UX designer</h3>
					<p>
						I focus on the small things that make shopping feel easy and pleasant —
						layouts, spacing, copy, and the way each product card invites you to look
						closer. If the site feels like it was made for you, that's the goal.
					</p>
				</li>
				<li>
					<h3>Lead developer</h3>
					<p>
						I build the code behind Agentic Fashion — from product listings and
						responsive layouts to a clean, consistent store experience that holds up
						across every view on every device.
					</p>
				</li>
			</ul>
		</section>

		<section>
			<div class="section-heading">A little of myself, with jokes</div>
			<div class="about-jokes">
				<p>
					If AI had to write a business plan, it would probably call itself "The Fashion
					Company" — and honestly, that's basically the whole point of this place. I don't
					worry about the AI being perfect. I just want it to make clothes that feel like
					they belong to you.
				</p>
				<p>
					I once designed a checkout flow that accidentally taught the AI to be extra
					friendly. I think that's the most useful thing the AI could do for you: making
					the whole process feel a little less like a chore.
				</p>
				<p>
					The reason I love this work is that every product page is a tiny conversation
					between design and clothing — and it always ends with a better fit.
				</p>
			</div>
		</section>

		<section class="about-cta">
			<div>
				<h2>See the collection</h2>
				<p class="about-cta__text">
					From outerwear to everyday essentials, the products are built to fit your style
					and your day.
				</p>
			</div>
			<a href="/shop" class="btn btn--primary btn--lg">Shop All Products</a>
		</section>
	</div>
</StoreLayout>
<style>
	.page-head__subtitle,
	.about-list,
	.about-jokes
	{
		margin: 0 auto 25px;
	}
	.about-cta {
		margin: 75px auto 25px
	}
</style>